\import{fdip-macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}
\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Remark}
\title{Orthonormal matrices for principal angles}
\date{2026-11-10}

\p{Choose orthonormal bases of the selected space and of an
eigenspace in the [invariants of a selected background](fdip-005J),
and let #{B_X} and #{B_\lambda} be the corresponding inclusion
matrices. Their product #{B_X^*B_\lambda} is the matrix of the
overlap. Replacing either basis multiplies this matrix on the left
or on the right by an orthogonal matrix, which does not change its
singular values.}

\p{TauCeti's \leanref/tauceti{TauCeti.cosPrincipalAngles} defines
the singular values of the overlap of two finite orthonormal
families as a nonincreasing sequence padded by zeros. Its first
#{\min(\dim X,\dim E_\lambda)} values, followed by arccosine, give
the angles above. Its
\leanref/tauceti{TauCeti.cosPrincipalAngles_le_one} supplies the
upper bound. Background conjugacy and the incidence claims are
separate arguments.}
